  // previous: 0.39.269 —   // [0.39.269: James — "i have no idea what ollama is doing" · "look at copilot" · "i want to be able to talk to copilot and ask what its been up to. agents tab in idearium is meant to build chunks, entire code bases. the agent hat is meant to be agnostic, ollama/guardian/copilot" · "guardian isn't capturing the code from chatgpt" · "the eravos options need to be removed from this prompt" · "ollama is supposed to have persistent memory ... using the download manager" · "you patch it. make sure you follow the axioms". 0.39.267: copilot's self-test was ALL of Ollama's work (6 generations/min, a third of wall time) → 1 call per run every 10 min (NEXUS_ADVERSARIAL_INTERVAL_MS); intuition crashed on 'what is X' and every blueprint answer (_getBP undefined) — fixed; vector-memory's health check POSTed /api/tags → GET; copilot/lib/activity-recall.js answers 'what have you been up to' from records (GET :3750/api/activity); lib/agent-providers.js is the one provider list (copilot, ollama, guardian userscripts on disk); chunk and codebase builds wear the repo hat (else the_builder) on the repo's Agent-tab switch; RAID's intent contract reads the worn hat. 0.39.268: all five guardian userscripts read replies with ``` fences put back (_replyText) and extractCode accepts the rendered-label form — code was lost at capture; ChatGPT's A/B chooser holds a job instead of stranding it; a code-less retry says so; builds use the default 3b, not the 7b; no Eravos mods in New Spec. 0.39.269: lib/agent-memory.js — agent memory IS the Clear Glass download manager: record() on every backend through response-sink + the chat index + chat-logger, recall() before every call (the agent's own exchanges + files built in its compartment + semantic chat_log); the ollama bridge records every real job; copilot, the Agent tab (new 'memory' block) and chunk builds recall; guardian honours hatInPrompt. Axioms pass (CLAUDE.md): mapped in docs/2026-09-27-agent-hat-memory-download-