  // previous: 0.39.258 —   // [0.39.258: James, live — "progress. didn't work a second time. the paste, shouldn't be injecting. only injecting the persona and the .inject nodes set in the agent tab and settings" / "not to inject anything into it that i cant edit in the agent settings". (1) The second job waited forever: a transcript completion handed ncp-handler the chat URL as the conversation-log session id; on Windows mkdir('…\\https:\\chatgpt.com\\…') threw ENOENT after job.status='complete' but before guardian.job.complete, so the pool never released the tab. The id is now the URL's last segment, lib/queue.js/ico.js make any id one safe folder name, and a log failure never stops a completion. (2) The paste carried three layers nobody could edit: the userscript's [NEXUS CONTEXT] (a repo hat's deliberately empty persona read as "no hat"), copilot's tool-loop system prompt (identity line, ALWAYS line, tool guide, USER: labels, whole-history re-paste), and the [NEXUS] "hey nexus" footer — which is why ChatGPT answered "hey nexus, 👋". Now the prompt is exactly lib/repo-prompt-blocks.js: persona, @learn, .inject, tool syntax, tool guide, matched code, project map, question, tool-result frame — each on/off and fully editable in Settings → Agents ("what the agent is sent", with a preview of the exact first message); {placeholders} are the only data filled in. Composed jobs get nothing from copilot (composed mode), guardian userscripts or the mesh wake hint. guardian 3.14.0 -> 3.15.0, copilot 3.6.0 -> 3.7.0, idearium 4.7.0 -> 4.8.0; userscripts chatgpt/claude 10.9.0, gemini/perplexity/deepseek 10.8.0. The "copilot" position asks copilot (GET /api/prompt/resolve) which backend its default is and sends the composed prompt there — copilot picks who answers, never what is sent; unresolvable = nothing sent. The "where does this code go?" side question is the editable inject-resolve block, sent alone. Tests: test-composed-prompt 20/20, 15 mutations each caught; Chromium probe of the new area 13/13; 21 related suites identical to baseline apart from the intended updates.]   // [0.39.257: James — "the toolscope for the agents tab. need the full capabilities, with the /help and tool awareness to help. need the commands as user friendly as possible. including debugging, using the intelligence system … also context on by default and wire in the graph"; asked which tools: "i want everything, at least for now." The repo agent sent a plain prompt, so it had NO tools (its hat listed 21, unenforced; ChatGPT saw read_file only). Now it runs copilot's real tool loop on ollama and browser agents: every registered tool (102) by default, or the hat's own set with /scope project — ENFORCED (runToolLoop allowedTools); the hat is the identity; file tools work in the repo's own files (lib/agent-tools/tool-root.js, context.repoDir) or NEXUS with where:nexus; the Agent tab shows each tool call. /help regrouped in plain language with aliases and closest-match; /tools (lib/agent-tools/tool-catalog.js: every tool grouped, none left over), /debug (syntax, unresolved imports, recent failures, intelligence_query/fault_log/diagnose) and /debug <question> (the agent investigates with the intelligence system), /graph, /run /test /diagnose. Context was already on by default; 'hello' got nothing — now the project map from graph.json, and matched chunks come with how their files connect. Found on the way: a failed tool-loop round was returned as the answer text; lifeline re-sent a prompt whose round failed; copilot .injection nodes and chat logs escaped the test sandbox. copilot 3.5.2 -> 3.6.0, idearium 4.6.1 -> 4.7.0. Tests: test-agent-tools-and-graph 13/13, 13 mutations each caught.]   // [0.39.256: James — "supposed to stream it live as it happens. do you think a delay between gates would help? like even just 500 ms?" / "can we make the error specific to the gate? not just a generic error?" A delay between gates would only slow every job: nothing streamed because the userscript's reply watch anchored on the composer (reply 0ch) and never sent a chunk. The 500 ms went where it helps — each userscript reads the reply from the transcript every 500 ms while it holds a job and sends GUARDIAN_CHUNKs (the reply is the assistant turn after the job's own user turn; a non-continuation is sent whole with reset; it yields when the watch streams). guardian/lib/gate-trail.js joins queued/dispatched/progress/chunk/timeout/error/complete into one trail per job; /status serves it; ask.js failures say 'stopped at gate 7/8 "reply appears" (chatgpt): … — <what to do>' and a dispatcher-failed job returns at once instead of after the timeout; the Agent tab shows gate rows and streams the reply live. guardian 3.13.0 -> 3.14.0, idearium 4.6.0 -> 4.6.1. Tests: test-live-stream-and-gates 13/13 incl. Chromium 8/8; 13 mutations each caught.]   // [0.39.255: James, after 0.39.254 worked live — "the hat should be repo specific not builder. the agent tab, in idearium is looking for the hash". The transcript held the ERAVOS agent's reply 12 s after dispatch, but was filed "(your chat)" (the job reported chat /c/WEB:c5f7a5cc…, the transcript came from /c/6ab7275b… — ChatGPT's temporary id) and the job never completed, so the Agent tab's late watch (a kind 'chat' .response with this job_id) had nothing to find, and the next job ("test") waited behind it in the one-job-per-tab pool. Now a chat is filed under the job whose prompt is one of its user turns, and a settled, not-generating transcript completes that job through the one GUARDIAN_COMPLETE path (every sink: .response with job_id → findLate → the Agent tab; guardian.job.complete; the pool) after GUARDIAN_JOB_DONE stops the tab's watch; a late tab error cannot undo it. Repo jobs wear their repo hat (repo_<slug>, persona already in the prompt, no second hat line), never the_builder. lib/chat-logger.js honours the test sandbox (it wrote data/chat-logs from every suite reaching completion). guardian 3.12.0 -> 3.13.0. Tests: test-chat-transcripts 31/31 incl. real Chromium 10/10 and an end-to-end transcript → real handler → findLate; 12 mutations each caught.]   // [0.39.254: James — "we were working on getting the download manager logging agent chats"; asked: a full-transcript sync, one record per chat (versioned), every provider chat incl. the userscripts in his own browser — "i want nexus to help remember. persistent memory for ai agents." A chat reached the downloads index only when a job COMPLETED; the live log had four ChatGPT jobs, none completed, zero .response nodes on disk. Now: provider userscripts (chatgpt/claude 10.6.0, gemini/perplexity/deepseek 10.5.0) push GUARDIAN_TRANSCRIPT when the chat settles and changed; every /sync result recorded too; guardian/lib/chat-transcripts.js writes through clear-glass artifact-chat-index recordChat (kind transcript, chat_key provider:chatId, version, transcript_hash; unchanged/contained-in-latest refused by name; every version kept). Whose chat: tab stamp > the job that ran in it (guardian.job.progress chatUrl) > already filed. Recall: guardian GET /api/chats (?agentId ?provider ?q), /api/chats/versions, /api/chats/item/:id. Library → Responses shows each chat once, as a conversation with its versions. Fixed: userscript-chatgpt chatId() stopped at the colon of /c/WEB:<uuid> (every chat read as WEB). guardian 3.11.1 -> 3.12.0, clear-glass 3.14.1 -> 3.15.0. Tests: test-chat-transcripts 20/20 incl. real Chromium 9/9, Library probe 29/29; 11 mutations each caught.]   // [0.39.253: James: \"i want the cli in idearium to be like the 3 way cli in the floating menu cli in the tv ui. that way it doesn't use check box. also have ollamas models to choose from in a drop down menu for the agent tab.\" Idearium's Agent tab CLI (and Settings → Agents) get the TV shell's three-way switch ollama · copilot · guardian instead of the guardian checkbox (copilot = stored provider 'auto'); a dropdown only where there is a choice — guardian agents, or Ollama's installed models (GET /api/ollama/models via the bridge; unreachable is said, never guessed). Per-compartment ollamaModel, validated against the installed list, sent as model on ollama dispatches only; copilot /api/prompt now passes it on (it dropped it). CLI /model. idearium 4.6.0, copilot 3.5.2. test-repo-agent-provider 60/60. NOT DONE: Chromium click-through of the switch.]   // [0.39.252: James — agent "hey nexus" is the agents' channel to NEXUS through Clear Glass, not the person's: "is supposed to be injected into the chat like a job." Three answerers, none complete: the page (nexus-wake checkMessage) matched the first streaming fragment ("hey nexus, w"), drew an overlay and typed the answer into the composer unsent; Clear Glass's wake-relay answered the same fragment again as a job that queued behind the unfinished reply; guardian's wake-loop (completed reply, depth cap, once per job) only ran for mesh jobs. Now wake-loop answers every agent wake once, from the completed reply, as a wake-reply job typed and sent into the same tab (pinned ncp), framed [NEXUS] answer to your "hey nexus, …". checkMessage reports only (nexus-wake 1.1.0); the relay returns on role assistant. Depends on the reply being detected (the open ChatGPT break). guardian 3.11.0 -> 3.11.1, clear-glass 3.14.0 -> 3.14.1. Tests: guardian-wake 16/16, nexus-wake NW-027/030, each fix mutation-checked.]   // [0.39.251: handoff 2026-09-25 step 1 — the element picker assigns selectors. A pick on a provider page (guardian-picker.js now reports guardian.picker.picked; one added line, look untouched) is offered as that provider's reply / input / send. clear-glass/renderer/selector-check.js generates a stable selector in the page and checks it the way the userscript reads it (resp: last match = the pick, no nesting, has text, a selector matching every reply beats a one-off; input/send: exactly one match, editable/button); a pick on an older answer is refused; one reply on the page = single, the person chooses among the passing candidates. src/providers/selector-assign.js refuses anything without evidence or with evidence from another provider's page, then POSTs guardian /api/agents/:id/selectors source picker. Area renderer/selector-assign/ (one JS + one CSS). Fixed on the way: guardian-picker xpaths through svg (send icons) never resolved via document.evaluate; archaeology.handlePick named every pick pick-1. Clear Glass 3.13.2 -> 3.14.0. Proven in real Chromium 141: selector-check 10/10, the area's whole flow 9/9; test-cg-selector-assign 10/10.]   // [0.39.250: records only — guardian spec built_2026_09_25_selector_map + atlas section, Versionium entries for 0.39.248 (vtm-eebbc621) and 0.39.249 (vtm-a91834dc), docs/2026-09-25-handoff.md. No code change.]   // [0.39.249: James: element picker aware of ClearDriver/userscripts/mesh, automatic DOM mapping, copilot able to fix it — "lets do it." MAPPED: guardian/lib/agent-registry.js already held one selector map per provider (input/send/resp + history with source/evidence) and the mesh's archaeology repair wrote to it, but the mesh path is off by default and the userscripts hard-coded their own selectors, so no repair ever reached the path jobs take. BUILT (step 1 of the plan): guardian/lib/selector-map.js — mapFor (each key verified only if its last change came from a live-checked source: picker, archaeology), assign (known keys only; a claimed live check without evidence is refused; pushes to every open tab of the provider), GUARDIAN_SELECTORS pushed on every NCP connect; GET/POST /api/agents/:id/selectors; userscript-chatgpt 10.5.0 precedence verified map > built-in > seed, a malformed map selector cannot break the watch. Tests: NEW test-selector-map 15/15 (real registry + module; the userscript's real functions), mutation-checked; correlation 120. NOT DONE: the picker UI that assigns a role in Clear Glass, automatic repair on no-reply-element, the other userscripts, guardian registry/contract entries for the two routes.]   // [0.39.248: the two boot VITALS CHECK FAILED items, both pre-existing (identical on 0.39.236), neither from 0.39.247's dispatcher work. (1) tests/dispatcher-stale-socket.test.js passed 2/2 (DSS-001 is the 'delivered to zero clients' check itself) but never exited: guardian/lib/dispatcher.js _armCompletionWatch's per-job watchdog timer kept the process alive until it expired, so the vitals runner timed the test out and reported FAIL. The timer is now unref'd -- it still fires in guardian (the HTTP server keeps that process up); it just no longer holds a process open by itself. (2) copilot-provider-toggle T-018 read a fixed 900-char slice of copilot/server.js and failed on correct code once the block's comments grew; it now reads to the block's end and also asserts no fall-through to lifeline.route(). Vitals 9/9 (was 7/9). Also: this line read 0.39.244 while package.json and the changelogs were at 0.39.247 -- 0.39.245-247 never moved it; corrected by this bump. NOT DONE: ChatGPT reply detection (mutations 4, reply 0ch, chat URL c/WEB:...) waits on the live DOM dump from James.]   // [0.39.244: James — the Agent tab's "hello" failed instantly ("guardian unavailable or returned no real response"), and "the cli in the agents tab needs to have a live feed of the dom mutation/node anchor". (1) copilot/lifeline.js and guardian/ask.js refused a repo job because the SHARED provider tab wasn't connected, though the job goes to the repo's OWN tab, which guardian's dispatcher opens itself — skipped for an agentId job; reasons and jobId now travel up (copilot's 502 carries jobId). (2) The Agent tab lost awaitLate: api() threw the refusal body away — kept on e.data. (3) guardian /events frames carried no payload, so idearium's live complete/error subscription never fired — guardian.job.* frames now carry a compact payload with agentId. (4) Five provider userscripts report the node they read (_nexusAnchor), mutation counts and a 1/s dom pulse; idearium relays repo-agent frames (SSE only); the Agent tab shows them live. See CHANGELOG-0.39.244.md.]
